[Music]  20:17 has been home to a bunch of  platformers inspired by a very special  era of games a hat and time poi and  ukulele have all had their time to shine  and there's this thing called super  mario odyssey releasing very soon maybe  you've heard of it but these games all  have one thing in common they take cues  from the platforming greats of the  Nintendo 64 so we're gonna count down  the top 9 platformers from Nintendo's  rad retro console some of these are  no-brainers some might surprise you and  others you might not even remember but  it all starts with number 9 Space  Station Silicon Valley DMA design is  better known today as Rockstar North yes  this cutesy platformer is from the same  team that went on to create the  blockbuster Grand Theft Auto series but  before players took control of Niko  Bellic or Trevor Phillips they  controlled a robot who crash-landed on a  space station more accurately they  control the robots little microchip  which could be used to jack into various  animals to complete levels across the  stations for different environments some  animals were faster some were stronger  but you had to use the whole zoo if you  wanted to get through this one number 8  spider-man spider-man is the only  licensed game you'll find on this list  and it absolutely earns its place for  the first time Spidey fans could swing  crawl and beat up bad guys in an open 3d  environment the comic-book vibe is  definitely here in spades too each level  is an issue of the spider-man comic  series with some sweet cover art in  loading screens and as far as villains  there are oh so many to fight here if  you're a fan of the multiverse Spidey's  like spider-man 2099 or The Scarlet  Spider you'll be happy to know that you  can unlock plenty of alternate costumes  for the webslinger too number 7 go  Iman's great adventure and now we get to  talk about our only 2.5 D choice after  going full 3d two years before the  mystical ninja series went back to the x  and y-axes with gell-mann's great  adventure but the levels still have much  to explore with multiple paths and even  side quests to complete as you make your  way from left to right  you can even go on the  sure with a friend in co-op mode and you  might need the help since the game's  day/night cycle brings out faster and  tougher enemies once the Sun Goes Down  number six  jet force Gemini this is the first game  from developer rare on this list but you  can be sure it's not the last jet force  Gemini is part platformer part shooter  fusing together elements of earlier rare  games like banjo-kazooie and Goldeneye  the Gemini team has to take down the  evil insectoid Mizar a mission that  involves multiple planets and nonlinear  levels across the galaxy having a trio  of heroes on the team also means  switching up control and using special  powers to breathe underwater or cross  lava and of course it wouldn't be a  platformer shooter hybrid without some  multiplayer deathmatches number 5  Conker's Bad Fur Day I'm sure you've  noticed that this list has been very kid  friendly but Conker's Bad Fur Day is  absolutely not that rare went a very  different direction from its other games  here at least thematically sure it's a  platformer at heart but conker drinks  heavily pees on fires and helps bees and  bucks and flowers get busy leaning back  on the shooter mechanics of jet force  Gemini it also offers a pretty lengthy  shooting segment that pokes fun at  Saving Private Ryan and of course that's  just one of many many parodies conker  offers I mean the final boss is a  combination of alien and Super Mario  64's Bowser fights number 4 banjo tooie  it might be weird to talk about the  sequel first but don't worry we'll get  to banjo kazooie soon the follow up  cranks the imagination of the first game  up to 11 with levels like Hellfire Peaks  which is a split between a fire and an  icy side and cloud cuckoo-land a sky  level with a bunch of weird floating  islands and while a lot of 3d  platformers force you out to a hub world  in between levels banjo tooie  interconnected worlds are still  impressive to this day sometimes you  even have to find those secret passages  in order to collect everything the  burden bear also get a huge list of new  powers during the journey not to mention  a multiplayer mode featuring all the  minigames you'll encounter along the way  number three Donkey Kong 64 before  banjo-tooie  rare brought one of Nintendo's main  mascots into 3d with DK 64 along with  that came a totally redesigned DK island  and a handful of simply massive levels  too much for just Donkey Kong a Cocker  on his own  fortunately you also get to control  other members of DK's family Diddy tiny  lanky and chunky Kong and I think we  know who the standout is there and of  course each member of the family has  their own set of powers and items to  help you collect every delicious banana  but beyond all the big levels and  special abilities Donkey Kong 64 has  stayed in our hearts for one very hip  reason number 2 banjo kazooie told you  we'd get to it soon banjo kazooie was  rares very first platformer on the n64  and it's definitely where the magic  started the Baron Byrd's first adventure  is so much more than just a series of  jumps and collectables levels aren't  just about getting from A to B they're  packed with unique characters like mumbo  jumbo a shaman who transforms you into  some crazy creature or contraption in  every level and the further you go the  more complex the worlds become the final  stage click clock would requires you to  rotate the world through spring summer  fall and winter to access certain parts  of the level banjo kazooie's showed just  how elaborate 3d platformers could be  and number one super mario 64 before any  other game on this list came Super Mario  64 the Plummers first foray and the 3d  totally changed how we perceive his  world stars weren't invincibility  power-ups anymore they were the main  collectible and collecting coins wasn't  just for a high score they also filled  Mario's health bar between bomb on  battlefield shifting sand land and so  many other levels you'd be hard-pressed  to find a game with more memorable  stages not to mention a fully explorable  Peach's castle with secrets of its own  Mario 64 paved the  for every 3d platformer to come just  like Super Mario Brothers did for 2d  platformers on the NES and there you  have it our top and 64 platformers of  all time what did you think of our  choices what games would be on your own  list let me know in the comments below  and if you liked this look back at older  games consider checking out our history  of series where we dive into big  franchises like Sonic the Hedgehog and  Uncharted  [Music]

